WEBVTT

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.590
Three hours to Shin-Osaka.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.460
We've sure got time to kill.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.200
Okay, Ono.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.600
Let's guess how many animals we'll see
outside by the time we get to Nagoya.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.200
Let me see...
I think we'll see ten animals.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.170
How about you, Ono?

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.010
Five?

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:47.640
Fifty?

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.110
Okay, let's see who gets closest.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.110
Loser gets tickled.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.090
All right, keep a lookout for any animals.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.890
Oh, there's some crows.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:03.290
One, two, three, four.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.430
This is looking bad.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:07.760
And those are horses.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.230
One, two.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.200
What the heck is that?

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.300
Well, we'll call it one animal.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:19.070
What? What the hell are those?

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:20.940
Are those even animals?

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:24.550
"Animal" is written as "a moving thing,"
so those must be animals.

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:29.520
Whoa, did you see that, Ono?
Those were colossal fish!

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.860
Is this Japan?
Are we really even in Japan?

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:40.300
Ghosts! It's an army of ghosts!

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.000
There are tons of them!

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:03.790
ORIGINAL WORK BY RENSUKE OSHIKIRI

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.410
APRIL 1996

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:35.040
As the teacher for the Ono family,
I have supported you for many years.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.010
But that will be ending soon.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.080
Akira...

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:43.950
Your parents living in Los Angeles
want you to go live with them there.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.160
You'll experience high school there.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:49.190
You'll graduate from university there.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:53.060
They want you to get used to
living in Los Angeles again.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.860
If possible,

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:01.400
I wanted to continue working here until
you graduated from university in Japan.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.210
When it comes to Ono family decisions,

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.910
I have no choice but to accept them.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.710
You'll attend the school chosen for you.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.710
You'll live where you're told to.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.820
You'll marry the man chosen for you.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.820
As the teacher for the Ono family,

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:21.420
I never felt anything wrong
with these decisions.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.230
At least, I did feel that way.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:29.060
My personal opinion is...

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:32.100
that these are regrettable decisions.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.040
<i>Shin-Osaka.</i>

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:43.910
<i>Shin-Osaka.</i>

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.550
You know what
the Osaka underground passages are?

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.960
They're like a complex game dungeon.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.960
So, where do you want to go, Ono?

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.030
Oh, Namba, is it?

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.630
Speaking of Namba,
that's the first stage of <i>Burning Fight</i>.

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.500
That's my only impression of Osaka
and all I know.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:12.840
Same with you, is it?

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:17.010
SNK's headquarters in Esaka is
in the opposite direction, though.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.480
What? You don't care?

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.620
That's it!

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:27.590
When you smash this in <i>Burning Fight</i>,
hot dogs come out!

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:31.260
What? You're afraid of it?
It must be the eyes.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.800
Since we arrived the day before
the competition,

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.830
let's check out some arcades
here in Osaka.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:42.200
Let's see what Kansai gamers can do
on their home turf.

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:47.980
This is my first time going to
an Osaka arcade.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.080
I'm so totally stoked!

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.780
What?

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:53.110
What is it?

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.450
You're too hungry to do that?

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.420
TAKOYAKI

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:03.460
In Tokyo, I got info on Osaka arcades.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:08.400
They said to look "under the bee"
between Tsutenkaku and Namba Station.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.470
I have no idea what that means.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.600
I know this thing.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.370
I've destroyed it in <i>King of the Monsters</i>.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.740
It's funny what this reminds us of.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.650
So, where is this "bee?"

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.620
Osaka has a bunch of sculptures and stuff,
so it must be something like that.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:36.090
We've come all the way to Osaka,
but we're not even visiting Tsutenkaku.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:39.430
Are you sure you're okay
with a trip like this, Ono?

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:41.100
You're okay with it.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:47.770
Okay, let's go.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.140
EBISUCHO STATION

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.470
A bee. A bee sculpture...

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:52.640
KETSUNE UDON

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.840
Alpha...

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.510
The arcade is called "Alpha" something.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:57.410
<i>Haruo!</i>

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.610
Oh, there it is!

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:05.420
Now that I think about it, there are still
a ton of games I haven't played you in.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:09.690
Never mind <i>Art of Fighting 1</i>.
But <i>Art of Fighting 2</i>,

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:13.060
the <i>World Heroes</i> series and
<i>Samurai Shodown</i>, we haven't played.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.530
<i>Street Fighter Alpha</i>
and <i>Street Fighter Alpha 2</i> too.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.470
There are all kinds of games
I haven't played with you, Ono.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:23.570
When all these new games were coming out,

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.340
we didn't have much money.

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:27.980
But not anymore!

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.680
I've got heaps of money now!

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.610
We'll make up for that lost time

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.820
with all the money I've raked in
at my part-time job!

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.020
What?

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:41.290
Not much charm in that.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:46.260
Here's one area
where the two of us have grown up.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:49.760
We talked about
the games we haven't played,

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:54.270
but we ended up playing
the latest game, <i>Last Bronx</i>.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:57.670
They turned gang fights into a video game.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.240
The best part is that
it's no-holds-barred.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:02.610
You sure you want the first game
you play in Osaka

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:05.350
to be a fight between gangs in Tokyo?

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.960
<i>As usual, she's real damn good.</i>

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:18.290
<i>When the heck does she practice?</i>

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:23.360
<i>Dang! She pulls off
the Custom Combo beautifully!</i>

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:28.140
<i>Her awesome talent hasn't changed a bit.</i>

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.840
<i>She wasn't mischievous like this either.</i>

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:35.610
<i>And I don't get upset at
every little thing. I've matured.</i>

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:40.080
Dang! Osaka arcades are intense!

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.750
Lately, it seemed like there was
less enthusiasm than back in the day.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:48.720
Seeing all these arcades around here
makes me feel better.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:51.890
It's been a while for you as well,
right, Ono?

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:54.560
I heard you were sneaking out
to arcades, though.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.130
There's no need to sneak around
in this town.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:00.470
You know,

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.310
I'm surprised that
Ms. Moemi let you go on this trip.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.710
I can't tell if she's strict
or a total pushover.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.480
You're totally in your element, Ono.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.620
I'm almost broke today.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.220
Let's go to the ten-yen arcade.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.220
I can't stand that Ferrari place, man.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.760
<i>It's been a while, so playing with Ono
has been a ton of fun,</i>

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.460
<i>but tomorrow's the competition.</i>

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.170
<i>In a lot of different ways,
it's an important match.</i>

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:35.900
<i>We should be spending the day
before getting prepared.</i>

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:40.940
<i>You know, we never have chances like this,
so just enjoy it.</i>

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.910
What? You're hungry again?

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.050
And you want takoyaki again?

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:47.880
You sure do love this stuff.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.220
What is it?

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.960
No. Don't do that kind of thing.

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:06.500
-That thing's on fire!
-<i>Haruo, I can't stand to watch!</i>

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:10.740
<i>These two used to fight like crazy!
What happened to them?</i>

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:13.040
<i>They had a lot of rough times,</i>

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.140
<i>but they're all fond memories now.</i>

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:20.450
<i>If we can, we want to watch you forever
from the sidelines!</i>

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:24.690
Hey, I picked up some valuable info
at that last arcade.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:30.090
<i>At the arcade, Ferrari, you can play
almost every game for only ten yen!</i>

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:35.600
Goddamn it!

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.060
Did you see that?

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:40.740
You can play for ten yen,
but they're on the toughest setting.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.400
And most of them are
set for single elimination.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:47.110
But if it were 50 yen,
that would be five fights.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.110
It's a total bargain
if you think of it that way.

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:52.680
WE HAVE A WINNER

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:53.850
<i>Game over!</i>

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.320
Can you believe that?

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.720
Here, a single blow can be deadly.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:01.590
Taking a single hit here is
totally different than at other arcades.

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:06.030
<i>If you want to win a fighting game,
don't get attacked.</i>

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:07.700
<i>It's the ultimate extreme style,</i>

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.030
<i>but that's the reality
on this battlefield.</i>

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:14.270
Gamers who honed their skills here
must have learned incredibly fast.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:19.440
Hey, it's been a while since we fought
in <i>Night Warriors</i>.

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:24.380
We still haven't settled on
who's better at this game.

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:29.350
<i>As usual, she's using
that weak character, Victor.</i>

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:34.020
<i>There's no way she has played lately,
so she must be rusty.</i>

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:37.830
<i>She must be, right?</i>

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:40.960
<i>She must be!</i>

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:46.830
What a loser!

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:49.670
How could Bishamon lose to
that weak-ass Victor?

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:53.810
This game is set up different!
It's single elimination!

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:57.340
-Hilarious!
-Ono really is a hell of an opponent.

00:11:57.750 --> 00:12:01.320
She blew me away instantly,
like I spent my ten yen on a slot machine.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.320
Now, this is an unusual girl.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:08.320
She puts up a pretty damn good fight.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:12.260
<i>What a weird feeling.</i>

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:15.530
<i>You bet it is. Do you remember
how you used to feel about her?</i>

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:19.000
<i>You said hanging around with her
always led to no good.</i>

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:21.070
<i>You even called her a pain in the ass.</i>

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:23.000
<i>But what about now?</i>

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:27.740
<i>I'm proud of her.</i>

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:30.710
What? What the hell?

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.580
You're just a softie for a girl.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:38.690
<i>She's so hot, the ten-yen coins of
these Osaka gamers melt like chocolate.</i>

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:42.120
<i>Being close to someone like her
just plain makes me happy.</i>

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:46.290
It's the Secret Garden!

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:49.530
You're only playing Rasputin
because you want to do that move!

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:55.370
<i>What's this?
That was a pretty aggressive nod!</i>

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:56.940
<i>I envy you, man!</i>

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:03.280
<i>Damn! She really is good
at fighting games.</i>

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:08.520
<i>Even without practice, she grasps
how to play and snatches away victory!</i>

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:11.450
<i>Can I really beat her tomorrow?</i>

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.460
I can't win at anything!

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:16.820
It's always like this, Miss Akira!

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:23.500
I bet you're trying to crush my confidence
the day before the competition!

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:24.730
But I won't let you!

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.870
No more fighting games for a while!

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.740
If we keep playing those,
it'll hurt my play tomorrow!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.640
<i>DIE HARD ARCADE</i>

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:35.940
How about Sega's new game,
<i>Die Hard Arcade</i>?

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:41.050
Wait! I don't mean alone.
Let's play together.

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:48.990
<i>She has gotten the better of you, Haruo!</i>

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:54.730
You know, it sure has been a while
since we played a co-op game, Ono.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:59.630
We used to play <i>Final Fight</i>
and <i>China Gate</i> together, though.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:04.240
For some reason, when I play with you,
we can clear every stage.

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:05.310
PRESS
JUMP

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.510
JUMP

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.940
<i>You're in perfect unison!</i>

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:11.710
You're doing great, Ono!

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:14.750
Let's complete this on our first play
with ten yen.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:16.680
<i>You haven't killed them yet?</i>

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.850
This is the terrorist group boss,
Wolf Hongo.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.990
It'll totally be worth killing him.

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:23.820
<i>Why isn't that safe opened yet?</i>

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:24.890
GET DOWN THERE! GET GOING!

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:29.200
And this is
the president's daughter, Caroline.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:33.000
Even gamers say they don't want to
save her, the poor girl.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.740
<i>Dang, this sure is fun.</i>

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:40.470
<i>What makes me happiest of all is</i>

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:42.180
<i>times like this.</i>

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:43.710
It's the cops!

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:45.950
The cops are coming!

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:46.910
What?

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:48.080
Get to the lobby!

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:52.920
The dynamite cops have arrived!

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.990
Any minors out playing around
after 10 p.m.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:57.930
will be hauled in and spanked!

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:01.600
-Say your prayers!
-Damn! We were having such a good time!

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:09.270
Well, we sure had a ton of fun
playing games.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:14.940
What?

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:18.050
Are you hungry?

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:21.320
You want to eat takoyaki?

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.820
<i>He still doesn't get it!</i>

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.600
What? Are you kidding?
The TV doesn't work!

00:15:41.070 --> 00:15:43.070
The damn thing's busted.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:46.370
<i>Jeez, I'm bored.</i>

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:50.710
<i>This is totally different than
when we were out playing in the arcades.</i>

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.310
<i>I'm totally bored.</i>

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:56.020
<i>There's absolutely nothing to do
in this room.</i>

00:15:56.680 --> 00:16:00.750
<i>I should have brought
my Game Gear or Game Boy.</i>

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.360
<i>It's tomorrow.</i>

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:07.530
<i>The </i>Super Street Fighter II Turbo<i>
national championships.</i>

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.400
<i>Are you sure you're okay?</i>

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:12.370
<i>It's the day before,
but you haven't practiced one bit.</i>

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:16.900
<i>I mean, I could lose
before I even get to Ono.</i>

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:21.380
<i>I totally imagined we would settle this
in the championship match.</i>

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:26.810
<i>If I lose in the first round,
will that mean I've lost to her?</i>

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:31.220
<i>It's also possible that
Ono will lose the first bout.</i>

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:34.220
<i>That sure would be unsatisfying
if that happened.</i>

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:38.030
<i>All I thought about was settling this
in a big competition.</i>

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:42.400
<i>But it just reduces the possibility
of defeating Ono.</i>

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:46.570
<i>Maybe we should have
just had a match in Mizonokuchi.</i>

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:52.540
<i>No! It's fitting that we settle this
at this big competition!</i>

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:56.140
<i>It's the fitting place for a showdown
after all these years!</i>

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:01.680
<i>She still isn't asleep?</i>

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:06.390
<i>After all the playing and eating she did,
I thought she would be exhausted.</i>

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.260
<i>I can hear everything she's doing!</i>

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:13.630
<i>The walls must be paper-thin
in this hotel.</i>

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:17.460
<i>What? She's eating chips.</i>

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.600
<i>There's zero privacy here.</i>

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:22.200
Hey, Ono! I bet you're eating chips!

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:25.970
Even after all the snacking you did today?
I can hear everything!

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:28.880
<i>Whoa, you're getting rough!</i>

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:32.310
<i>You know she can't snack at home.</i>

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:34.880
<i>This is a weird feeling,</i>

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:39.020
<i>knowing that Ono is right on
the other side of this wall.</i>

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:43.260
<i>After so many twists and turns,
she's so near.</i>

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.830
<i>It's hard to believe.</i>

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:52.970
<i>Even though I need to get to bed early
for tomorrow,</i>

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:54.800
<i>I'm not the least bit sleepy.</i>

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.510
<i>It must be the nervousness
about tomorrow's big match.</i>

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:01.310
<i>No.</i>

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:04.310
<i>It's because Ono's in the next room.</i>

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:06.910
<i>I can't help thinking about her.</i>

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:12.750
<i>I know I've got to get to sleep soon,
so what's wrong with me?</i>

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:16.190
<i>No, I'm not waiting.</i>

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:18.430
<i>Liar.</i>

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:22.800
<i>No. I'm not waiting for Ono to come over.</i>

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:24.200
<i>You damn liar!</i>

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.300
<i>I'll admit, I'm totally bored,</i>

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:30.270
<i>and it would be fun to
talk with Ono, but...</i>

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:34.580
<i>Well, even though she doesn't say a word.</i>

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:38.080
<i>She must be asleep by now.</i>

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:42.020
<i>So, how does this other me look to you?</i>

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:44.590
<i>Brown Guile!</i>

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:46.190
<i>Why are there two Guiles?</i>

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:52.330
<i>This is the "turtling Guile"
that I imagine is the state of her heart.</i>

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:55.300
<i>This is the portrait of hesitation!</i>

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.900
<i>That's right. She's waiting.</i>

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.340
<i>She's waiting for you to go into her room!</i>

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:07.370
<i>Let's see if you're right.</i>

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:08.280
<i>Good!</i>

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:12.580
<i>-Sonic boom!
-Sonic boom!</i>

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:14.080
<i>It's no good, Haruo!</i>

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:15.820
<i>She's too damn stubborn!</i>

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:16.980
<i>You!</i>

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:18.790
<i>You make the move!</i>

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:22.290
<i>Pluck up your courage and get in there!</i>

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:32.370
Hey, Ono, aren't you frightened all alone?

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.670
Aren't you worried about ghosts?

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:37.940
Have you checked the back of
the picture frame?

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:41.710
What? No way!

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:44.480
What happened? Did you really see a ghost?

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:51.020
Holy crap, it's the real deal.

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:54.790
I was only joking. Who would've thought
there would really be one?

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:57.960
Jeez, it's busted to pieces.

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:00.190
The hotel will get angry, you know.

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:04.130
It figures you would be angry too,
for being given this room.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:08.200
As usual, you still can't handle
things like this.

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:11.270
You're already a high-school sophomore.

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:12.840
Get over it, would you?

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:24.350
The competition is tomorrow,
so get to bed, all right?

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:26.350
That hurts!

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.860
And get over
throwing tantrums like that too!

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:32.390
PLEASE CLEAN THE ROOM

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:35.030
Ono, it's already 1 a.m.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:39.470
Unless we get to sleep,
it'll hurt us in tomorrow's competition.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:44.000
<i>This girl really is silent.</i>

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:47.870
<i>Actually, I probably just hate silence.</i>

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:50.340
<i>The TV's busted,</i>

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:52.750
<i>so talking to Ono's the only thing to do.</i>

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:54.920
<i>I'll escape!</i>

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:59.190
Ono, I'll go sleep
in your ghost-infested room.

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:01.960
You can sleep in my...

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:08.960
You really are like

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:11.060
a little kid.

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:16.000
<i>Tomorrow, this scaredy-cat is</i>

00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:19.870
<i>going to face off against
the best in the country with Zangief.</i>

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:22.740
<i>I could worsen the damage done to her</i>

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:25.150
<i>by that talisman on the picture frame
so that I win tomorrow.</i>

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:28.080
<i>But that wouldn't be fair.</i>

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:31.180
<i>Ono, have you taken a bath?</i>

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:34.220
<i>Good. Did you brush your teeth?</i>

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:36.720
<i>Good. Well done.</i>

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:42.160
Then let's get to sleep quick
so we're ready for tomorrow.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:48.700
<i>Haruo!</i>

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:51.170
<i>I've always faced off against this guy.</i>

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:56.040
<i>And do you remember how
the brown version of me was there tonight?</i>

00:21:58.550 --> 00:22:01.620
<i>But now, I'm facing a lady.</i>

00:23:36.610 --> 00:23:37.580
RICE BALL ERASER

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:42.380
<i>I wonder why we can't always
do our best during a competition.</i>

00:23:42.780 --> 00:23:45.790
<i>Sometimes, you can't defeat someone
who's usually a breeze to beat.</i>

00:23:45.850 --> 00:23:48.720
<i>While other times,
you face someone you never beat, but...</i>

00:23:49.720 --> 00:23:51.390
<i>No, you still can't beat them.</i>

00:23:52.030 --> 00:23:53.060
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
